# Lychee URL exclusions for the markdown-links CI job.
# Each entry is a Rust regex matched against the full URL. Add a one-line
# comment above the entry explaining why it is excluded. See Issue #10.

# nestjs-zod GitHub repo: the package author's handle has rotated; the
# `risenforces/nestjs-zod` URL cited in ADR-0002 (EN+RU narrative+design,
# 4 occurrences) returns 404. The npm registry (https://www.npmjs.com/
# package/nestjs-zod) is the stable, content-addressed reference; the
# GitHub URL is kept inline for historical context but lychee ignores it.
^https://github\.com/risenforces/nestjs-zod($|/.*$)

# Org-level Projects v2 boards under doctor-school: project boards are
# private, so lychee (unauthenticated) gets 404 even when the project
# exists. The URL is useful for owner / agent navigation; verified
# manually rather than by CI. DSP-198 board #1 is the current example.
^https://github\.com/orgs/doctor-school/projects/.*$

# npmjs.com scoped-package pages: the registry returns 403 Forbidden to
# lychee's unauthenticated user-agent for scoped packages (e.g.
# @stoplight/spectral-owasp-ruleset, cited in the endpoint-authz-matrix
# design spec). The page exists and is content-addressed; verified
# manually. Same false-positive class as the nestjs-zod entry above.
^https://www\.npmjs\.com/package/@stoplight/spectral-owasp-ruleset($|/.*$)

# Imported Claude Design source (design-source/): reference material, not a
# runnable app. (1) The provenance links in its README point at the login-gated
# Claude Design canvas, which unauthenticated lychee cannot reach. (2) The
# imported ds-foundation.dc.html references the canvas-side runtime + logo assets
# (support.js, assets/ds-logo-*.svg) that we intentionally do NOT vendor (see the
# folder README). Both are verified manually / re-pullable via DesignSync — same
# false-positive class as the private Projects v2 boards above.
^https://claude\.ai/design/.*$
design-source/assets/
design-source/support\.js

# GOV.UK Design System: the site's WAF resets TCP connections from
# GitHub-hosted (Azure) runner IPs — `Connection reset by peer (os error 104)`,
# reproduced twice on PR #1227 — while the page answers 200 in <1s from a
# residential connection. Cited in design/constitution.md; verified manually.
# Same crawler-hostile false-positive class as the npmjs 403 entry above. #1228
^https://design-system\.service\.gov\.uk($|/.*$)

# GitHub Primer, GitHub's own design system — cited in design/constitution.md at
# three places (button states, form errors, segmented control). Excluded because
# it is FLAKY, not because it is down: on 2026-08-14 three CI runs on one branch
# with NO change to the tree between them produced `markdown-links` red, red,
# then green — the two reds reporting three `Timeouts` and zero `Errors` on the
# same three URLs. Residential probes hung on both `/product/` pages across the
# entire window, including at the moment the green run passed, so this is
# neither a regional split nor a clean site-down; earlier in the same window
# `/ui-patterns/forms/` returned 502 and the domain root hung. A nondeterministic
# third-party dependency on a BLOCK gate is worse than a steady red — it gates
# merges at random — so the exclusion is domain-wide and does NOT lapse when the
# site next answers. Not a stale citation: Primer's own redirect from
# `/components/button` targets the hanging `/product/components/button/`, so the
# cited URLs are canonical. In the tree since 2026-07-01 (f4c46f72, PR #415) and
# green in CI until today. Owner decision 2026-08-14 (#1249): CI must not gate
# on a third party's availability. Same class as the GOV.UK entry above.
^https://primer\.style($|/.*$)

# Vendored Claude Design canvas sources (design-source/*.dc.html): verbatim
# spec artifacts, not documentation. Their {{ template }} hrefs and
# canvas-relative links (events-feed.dc.html, account-my-events.dc.html, …) resolve only
# inside the Claude Design project, never in this repo — lychee sees them as
# file:// links and reports false File-not-found errors (#514).
^file://.*/design-source/.*$

# THIS repository's own URLs (github.com/doctor-school/ds-platform/…): 3277
# occurrences / 858 unique across the tree (2026-10-13) — changesets-generated
# commit + PR links in every CHANGELOG.md, and Issue/PR/milestone citations in
# specs, ADRs, READMEs and DEBT.md. Excluded so the guard's verdict does not
# depend on several hundred requests to github.com per run; none of these
# links is known to be wrong, and none is verified by CI while excluded.
#
# Live behaviour (#2860, unauthenticated `curl -s -o /dev/null -w
# '%{http_code}' <url>`, 2026-10-13): the repository is public and its pages
# answer without credentials — repo root, /pull/1215, a CHANGELOG commit
# (/commit/4e48d2a9…), /commit/bc22c2c4 and /blob/main/AGENTS.md = 200;
# /issues/660 = 302 to /pull/660 (GitHub's Issue→PR redirect); 39 of a 40-URL
# sample of the unique set = 200, the 40th = 302. A wrong reference fails
# plainly: /issues/999999 = 404, and the raw form of a missing file = 404. In
# lychee v0.24.2 (lychee-lib/src/checker/website.rs) a successful plain
# request returns at once, so a valid self-URL never reaches the GitHub-API
# fallback that spends the workflow token's hourly budget.
#
# What keeping the exclusion still buys is determinism and run cost: each run
# would send one github.com HTML request per unique self-URL (858 today,
# growing with every CHANGELOG entry) from GitHub-hosted runner IPs, and
# github.com has already answered that runner with transient HTTP 503s on
# this same job (PR #2743, PR #2833 — the blob-view half was moved to
# raw.githubusercontent.com by #2747). A self-URL that hits a 503 or a
# rate limit and then fails the API fallback is reported with its ORIGINAL
# status (website.rs: the fallback's own error is discarded), so one bad
# minute on github.com would read as broken links on a BLOCK gate. Whether
# to re-include self-URLs — whole, or only the offline-checkable commit half
# (`git cat-file -t <sha>` on the full checkout) — is an owner decision
# recorded on #2860; the coverage gap is tracked in DEBT.md.
^https://github\.com/doctor-school/ds-platform($|/.*$)
# The same self-URLs in their raw form: the markdown-links step remaps every
# `github.com/…/blob/<ref>/<path>` citation to `raw.githubusercontent.com`
# (#2747), and lychee v0.24.2 matches exclusions AFTER the remap
# (lychee-lib/src/client.rs `check`: `self.remap(&mut uri)` precedes
# `self.is_excluded(&uri)`), so without this line this repo's own blob links
# would escape the exclusion above.
^https://raw\.githubusercontent\.com/doctor-school/ds-platform/.*$

# GOV.UK Ministry of Justice design-patterns site: since 2026-09 the host
# answers 401 Unauthorized to unauthenticated clients (lychee included),
# although the page opens in a browser. The citation in
# apps/docs/content/design/constitution.md (filter-a-list pattern) stays
# inline as a historical reference; verified manually, not by CI.
^https://design-patterns\.service\.justice\.gov\.uk($|/.*$)

# Yandex Cloud docs (smartcaptcha key format, cited in infra/deploy/README.md):
# the host answers 403 Forbidden to lychee from GitHub-hosted runners
# (PR #1913, run 33998232057, 2026-09-05) while the same URL returns 200 from
# a residential connection with and without a lychee user-agent. The link was
# in the tree before #1913 and is not part of its diff. Same crawler-hostile
# false-positive class as the npmjs / GOV.UK entries above; verified manually.
^https://yandex\.cloud($|/.*$)
